---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import '../styles/pages.css';
---

<Site title="Privacy Policy" description="Purple Directive privacy policy — how we handle your data when you use our website and purchase our products.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
    <div class="legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: September 25, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Purple Directive ("we", "us", "our") operates the website purpledirective.com.
      This page describes how we collect, use, and protect your information when you visit
      our site or purchase our products.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>When You Visit Our Site</h3>
    <p>
      We use two analytics tools. Neither sets cookies, and neither is used for advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Our own analytics.</strong> A small tracker served from
      analytics.purpledirective.com, running on our own server, records for each page view:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the page path (for example <code>/sop-bundle</code>)</li>
      <li>the site that referred you, as a host name only (for example linkedin.com)</li>
      <li>campaign tags in the link you followed (<code>utm_source</code>, <code>utm_medium</code>, <code>utm_campaign</code>)</li>
      <li>your country, as reported by Cloudflare's network</li>
      <li>device type, browser and operating system, read from your browser's user agent</li>
      <li>
        a visitor ID: a one-way hash of your IP address, your browser's user agent and
        the current date. Because the date is part of it, the ID changes every day, so
        visits on different days cannot be linked. Your IP address itself is not stored.
      </li>
      <li>
        whether the page is the first of your visit, noted in your browser's session
        storage for that tab only (cleared when the tab closes)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Clicks, masked session recordings and error reports.</strong> To find where
      pages confuse people or break, we also collect which links and buttons are clicked,
      and reports of errors in the page. We may also record a masked replay of how a page
      was used for a sample of visits: page text and anything typed are always hidden, and
      a replay may show page images (this site has no accounts, cart, or checkout — nothing
      personal is ever shown on a page here in the first place). None of this includes
      health information.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Short links.</strong> Links we share in posts and emails look like
      purpledirective.com/go/&hellip;. When you follow one, our server records the click
      with the campaign the link was made for (for example, a LinkedIn post) and a random
      click ID, then sends you to the page with that ID after a <code>#</code> in the
      address. The page reads the ID once, sends it with your visit so the visit can be
      matched to the link, keeps it in session storage for that tab, and removes it from
      the address bar. The ID is random and says nothing about you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics.</strong> Cloudflare, which hosts this site, also
      provides Cloudflare Web Analytics. It does not use cookies and reports aggregate page
      views and referral sources.
    </p>

    <h3>When You Make a Purchase</h3>
    <p>
      Purchases are processed through Stripe, a PCI-DSS Level 1 certified payment processor. When you
      purchase a product, Stripe collects your payment information (card number, billing
      address, email). We do not store your payment details on our servers. We receive your
      name and email address from Stripe in order to deliver your purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you click a buy button, our analytics records the click with a random join key,
      and the same key goes to Stripe with your checkout. Our record of the sale keeps that
      key, the campaign tags of the link you used, and your answer to &ldquo;How did you
      hear about us?&rdquo; if you gave one, so we can tell which pages and posts lead to
      sales. If you start a checkout and do not finish it, we record that the checkout
      expired, with the same campaign details and without your name or email address.
    </p>

    <h3>When You Contact Us</h3>
    <p>
      If you email us at info@purpledirective.com or use our contact form, we receive
      your name, email address, and message content. We use this only to respond to your inquiry.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To deliver products you purchase (email with download link)</li>
      <li>To respond to support requests or inquiries</li>
      <li>To understand how people find and use the site, and which pages, posts and links lead to purchases</li>
      <li>To find and fix pages that break or confuse people</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <table class="legal-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Service</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Data Shared</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Stripe</td><td>Payment processing</td><td>Payment details, email, name; the checkout's campaign tags and random join key</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Hosting, security, Cloudflare Web Analytics, short-link and buy-link redirects</td><td>Traffic passes through its network; analytics reported in aggregate</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Microsoft 365</td><td>Email delivery</td><td>Your email address (for purchase delivery)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Purchase records (name, email, transaction ID, and how you found us) are retained for
      accounting and tax purposes. Analytics records are kept on our own server. You may request deletion of your data by emailing
      <a href="mailto:info@purpledirective.com">info@purpledirective.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Our website does not set first-party cookies. Our analytics uses your browser's session
      storage, which is cleared when you close the tab, to note whether a page is the first of
      your visit and to hold a short-link click ID. Stripe may set cookies during the
      checkout process on their domain. Cloudflare may set a security cookie
      (<code>__cf_bm</code>) to distinguish humans from bots.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      All connections to purpledirective.com are encrypted via TLS (HTTPS). Payment
      processing is handled entirely by Stripe's PCI DSS Level 1 certified infrastructure.
      We do not store credit card numbers or CVVs.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our products and services are intended for clinical research professionals.
      We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page
      with an updated "Last updated" date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this privacy policy? Email us at
      <a href="mailto:info@purpledirective.com">info@purpledirective.com</a>.
    </p>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 680px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }

  .legal-page h1 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .legal-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .legal-page h2:first-of-type {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .legal-page h3 {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .legal-page p,
  .legal-page li {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-page ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: var(--spacing-sm) 0;
  }

  .legal-page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .legal-page a {
    color: var(--purple-primary);
  }

  .legal-page code {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: var(--bg-tinted);
    padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .legal-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
  }

  .legal-table th {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .legal-table td {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
